864,"","","","","","r","Driving (or taking the bus) across Gwangan Bridge is a great way to see the view, especially at nighttime. Viewed from the town it has an impressive light display at night. It featured in the Marvel movie 'Black Panther'."],["Millak subyeon park","sight",35.1549,129.13366,"361, Gwanganhaebyeon-ro","","","","","r","Here is a park where people can see Gwangan grand bridge and Gwangalli beach."],["Suyeong-gu Cultural Center","sight",35.1528,129.1245,"337-1, Gwanganhaebyeon-ro","Varies by event","","","","r","A community hub that hosts various performances, exhibitions, and cultural classes. It's a great place to experience local arts and culture."],["Gwangalli Marine Leisure Zone","activity",35.1521,129.1209,"Gwanganhaebyeon-ro","Seasonal","","","","r","A designated area offering seasonal marine leisure activities such as kayaking and paddleboarding, popular with visitors during summer months."],["Gwangalli Hoe Festival","activity",35.15417,129.12056,"","Held annually in October","","","","r","A raw fish festival held annually in October. The event, which takes place on the sandy expanse of Gwangalli Beach, is a lively celebration of Busan's seafood culture. Visitors can participate in a variety of activities, including…"],["Busan Fireworks Festival","activity",35.15417,129.12056,"","Held annually in October","","","","r","The Busan Fireworks Festival takes place every October along Gwangalli Beach, transforming the city's iconic shoreline into a dazzling spectacle of light and sound. Drawing millions of spectators each year, it stands as one of South…"],["Gwangan Bridge Walk","activity",35.154,129.125,"Gwangan Bridge","Held annually in May","","","","r","Each year, the Gwangan Bridge is opened to the public for a walking festival. This unique event allows you to walk or run across Busan’s most famous landmark, an opportunity not available at any other time of the year. The walk offers…"],["Millak Town Raw Fish Center","restaurant",35.15558,129.12379,"","Varies by stall","","","","r","Busan is famous for raw fish ('회 Hway'), which the Koreans eat in the same style as bulgogi, namely topped with kimchi and gochujang and wrapped in a lettuce leaf. One of the best places to sample this is in a large brown building at…"],["Four Season Raw Fish","restaurant",35.15558,129.12379,"","Varies by stall","","","","r","The owner, Mr. Jun, speaks English, and ordering here is easy: it's either set A, B or C. Even Set A is huge, while C is extremely large. This is as real as it gets and dishes will include still-moving octopus tentacles and other stuff…"],["Samho Fish Restaurant","restaurant",35.155,129.124,"","","","","","r","A local favorite for fresh sashimi and traditional Korean seafood stews. Known for its high quality and authentic flavors, often featuring seasonal catches."],["Millak Kalguksu","restaurant",35.1532,129.1247,"29-8 Millaksubyeon-ro","10:00-20:00","","","","r","A humble restaurant near Millak Port serving delicious handmade noodle soup (kalguksu) and pajeon (green onion pancake)."],["Hanoi Phở","restaurant",35.1585,129.1228,"59-13 Millak-ro","10:00-21:00","","","","r","A simple, no-frills Vietnamese restaurant serving excellent pho (beef noodle soup) and banh mi. Quick, delicious, and affordable."],["Café Knotted Gwangalli","restaurant",35.1532,129.1208,"Gwangannogbyeon-ro","10:00–22:00","","","","r","A popular dessert café known for its donuts and colorful interior, frequently visited by tourists and younger visitors walking along Gwangalli Beach."]]}